{"entryId":"1663","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1663:1","sourceSha256":"5bb44a28dba5ef5e11ccbcfa521718271827e54e64c04b6f21e38324451a12a1","englishSha256":"712e03d57cb1d724a0cffb536a6d98fddaa4f9020de100119f3ad30c3cc9ee53","citations":[{"id":"1663:1:citation-01","he":[14,48],"en":[46,64],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_33b.5.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 33b:5:1","assessment":"Rashi explicitly glosses the label as son of a male and a female convert.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 33b:5:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_33b.5.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1663:1:citation-02","he":[81,173],"en":[316,329],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_9a.20"},"reference":"Moed Katan 9a:20","assessment":"The Bavli has Yonatan ben Asmai and Yehudah ben Gerim study with Rabbi Shimon, who sends his son to them for a blessing. The checked Tosafot on Shabbat has Shimon ben Chalafta in citing the story. Keep the reported Akhmai and the competing readings.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 9a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_9a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Moed Katan 9a:23","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_9a.23"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 33b:5:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_33b.5.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1663:1:citation-03","he":[175,220],"en":[424,444],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_33b.5"},"reference":"Shabbat 33b:5","assessment":"The direct narrative says he repeated their words and the report reached the authorities. It does not say he personally informed on Rabbi Shimon to the king.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 33b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_33b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1663:1:citation-04","he":[241,260],"en":[479,507],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_33b.6"},"reference":"Shabbat 33b:6","assessment":"The checked Bavli gives two periods of twelve years and twelve months. Sheviit names thirteen years continuously in its separate account.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 33b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_33b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 33b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_33b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Sheviit 9:1:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Sheviit_9.1.13"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]},{"id":"1663:1:citation-05","he":[262,314],"en":[596,619],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_34a.2"},"reference":"Shabbat 34a:2","assessment":"The checked continuation says Shimon saw Yehudah when he went out to the market and turned him into a heap of bones. The separate preceding figure dies. Direct Tosafot prefers a death reading for Yehudah and rejects the bones wording. Keep both witnesses.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 34a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_34a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 34a:2:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_34a.2.4"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 33b:5:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_33b.5.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1663:1:citation-06","he":[262,314],"en":[621,635],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_33b.5.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 33b:5:1","assessment":"The checked continuation says Shimon saw Yehudah when he went out to the market and turned him into a heap of bones. The separate preceding figure dies. Direct Tosafot prefers a death reading for Yehudah and rejects the bones wording. Keep both witnesses.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Shabbat 33b:5:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Shabbat_33b.5.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Shabbat 34a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_34a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 34a:2:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_34a.2.4"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1663:1:citation-07","he":[380,432],"en":[816,843],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_35.3"},"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 35:3","assessment":"The checked Midrash counts a third participant, Yudan Giyori, and gives variant descriptions of what they studied. The exact separate Yerushalmi patronymic remains a hold.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 35:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_35.3"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,6],"holds":[{"raw":"ובירושלמי בר גיורי","reason":"The located Bereshit Rabbah witness names Yudan Giyori. The separate exact Yerushalmi locator remains open.","evidence":[]},{"raw":"כתב בנובלות חכמה (קצ\"ד ב')","reason":"Preserve the mystical account as an attributed quotation. A direct edition-bound reading of the cited folio is still needed.","evidence":[]}],"notes":[{"text":"Preserve the distinct accounts of the court report, the number of cave years and the death. The Novlot Chokhmah statement remains attributed.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 33b:5:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_33b.5.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Moed Katan 9a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_9a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Moed Katan 9a:23","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_9a.23"},